This '''Timeline''' is a rough estimation of the universe of [[Wuthering Waves]]. LD (Landing Date) refers to the year that [[Rover]] lands in [[Solaris-3]] and starts the game's events.

References are provided as much as possible.

==Pre-First Lament==
*'''?''' &mdash; [[The Farwatcher]] and eight other interstellar probes are launched by the [[Pre-Lament Civilization]].
*'''?''' &mdash; The Tethys Institute proposes, approves, and executes [[Resolution K626]] as the Lament begins.
==First Global Lament==
*'''10,000 years before LD''' &mdash; There have been five global [[The Lament|Laments]] and more than 300,000 regional Laments since 10,000 years before LD until LD.. The first Global Lament hit Solaris, rewriting the foundational of matter of the universe into frequencies. Gravity is the only pre-Lament law of physics that still applies.
*'''?''' &mdash; The [[Fractsidus]] is founded
*'''?''' &mdash; Rover arrives from the [[Homeland Civilization]] with the mission to stop the Lament on Solaris-3. The SkyArk space station, a [[Court of Savantae]] satellite, witnesses Rover falling through the [[Etheric Sea]]. The Etheric Sea is an atmospheric [[Waveworn Phenomenon|Waveworn Phenomena]] that blankets the globe and prevents humans from reaching outer space. [[Schwarzloch|Weiying]], one of the researchers aboard the SkyArk station, is the earliest confirmed identity of the Grand Architect.
*'''?''' &mdash; The [[Roya Frostlands]] becomes [[Solaris-3|Solaris's]] new pole following the first [[The Lament|Lament]] ever recorded, when its once-lush forests were transformed into an endless ice sheet.. The Roya live on this 
==Post First Lament==
===Second Lament===
**When the second recorded [[The Lament|Lament]] strikes the Roya Frostlands, [[Threnodian]] [[Aleph-1]]  - having arrived alongside the [[Exostrider]] from outer space- unleashes the [[Void Storm]]. The Exostrider resonates with [[Aemeath]] and seals Aleph-1 above Solaris-3, behind the [[Stridergate]]. This is the only remaining connection to outer space after the descent of the Etheric Sea. To counter the devastation caused by the overflow of Voidmatter, the Exostrider shed its own components and transformed them into the [[Exoswarm]], restoring [[Lahai-Roi]]'s damaged ecology. It also guided the [[Roya Tribe|Roya]] tribe to relocate their settlements in Lahai-Roi, beneath the frozen expanse. 
===Unknown Location===
*'''?''' &mdash; Rover makes enemies out of many organizations. One of said organizations creates [[Camellya]] to assassinate Rover. It is likely that this organization is behind her Resonance Awakening, as she is an Artificial Resonator.
*'''?''' &mdash; The Somnoire is created to store and analyze peoples' dreams and search them for potential solutions to the Lament. The [[Ivory Gatekeeper]] and [[Ebony Gatekeeper]] are created as the Somnoire's guardians, and Rover is granted the authority of "Dreamwalker" within its system.

===Black Shores===
*'''?''' &mdash; The Tethys System is created by an unknown civilization, likely the [[Homeland Civilization]].
*'''?''' &mdash; The Shorekeeper is created in a piece of light blue crystal made of remnant energy, gathered from the "Anchor" on the Black Shores Archipelago. Rover touches the crystal, and their frequency resonates with the crystal, awakening the [[Shorekeeper]] and allowing her to take a human form.
*'''?''' &mdash; Rover founds the [[Black Shores]] organization as a way to gather people to solve the Lament. Tethys selects the people that Rover recruits. The organization provides evacuation and support relief for locations devastated by the Lament, and brings back the Reverberation data for Shorekeeper to analyze.

